{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/584478-a-bit-left-behind","id":584478,"title":"A bit left behind?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-09T03:45:25-07:00","id":584478,"title":"A bit left behind?","content":"So vampires can spend blood to up stats, werewolves have their wereshape and demons have their form alteration as well. However all three also have the starting 3 dot this that or the other thing. Do Promethens seem a bit under powered? Sure they can kinda heal well but only in a modern setting with lots of power sources. <br /> If you took a Promethen and use pandoran abuilities and constructed for him an equivalent wereform you would eat up a LOT of xp while the demon and werewolf sail past your general effectiveness level. <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6424-fuzzykuma","name":"Fuzzykuma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T04:58:26-07:00","id":584523,"title":"","content":"They can also resist damage better than any of those, and even come back from the dead, so... we probably should wait to see what the innate capabilities of Prometheans are in 2nd edition so we aren't comparing apples and oranges.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T09:40:33-07:00","id":584833,"title":"","content":"First edition Prometheans can buff their stats as well. All of them, too, not just the physical ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T09:46:10-07:00","id":584839,"title":"","content":"Most also have the ability to spend a point of pyros to reroll a failed check (on a specific attribute, but still) which also enables them to go beyond 5 points in said attribute. And they don't really <i>need</i> a warform. It's not thematic at all for them. We also don't know about their Torment yet, they might become even more dangerous than a raging vampire when they go nuts (and bolts...I'll see myself out.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T14:02:59-07:00","id":585171,"title":"","content":"Plus Prometheans can heal themselves via electricity, some can heal with radiation. They can also turn their body into a living Tesla Coil when it comes to electricity so as to harm nearby non-prometheans.<br /> <br /> Prometheans only need to eat organic or inorganic (w/ merit) once per day. If food is scarce they can go up for three full days without food with no ill effects.<br /> <br /> Prometheans can have an astonishingly long lifespan if they haven't completed their pilgrimage.<br /> <br /> Prometheans can keep fighting/fleeing until ALL of their health boxes have aggravated damage. They do not need to make stamina rolls if their health boxes reach full bashing or full lethal. Even if they do die, they can come back to life. Then you also got to remember that Osirion prometheans or others who have purchased a slightly more expensive version of &quot;Revivification&quot; can keep coming back to life more than once.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6740-goblin-engineer","name":"Goblin Engineer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T12:30:17-07:00","id":587338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/584478-a-bit-left-behind?p=584839#post584839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most also have the ability to spend a point of pyros to reroll a failed check (on a specific attribute, but still) which also enables them to go beyond 5 points in said attribute. And they don't really <i>need</i> a warform. It's not thematic at all for them. We also don't know about their Torment yet, they might become even more dangerous than a raging vampire when they go nuts (and bolts...I'll see myself out.)</div> </div> </div> </div>This benefit is actually really underrated I think.<br /> It works mechanically simmilar to a Rote Action, but the wording is slightly different. The way I read it, you can keep spending Pyros multiple times, rerolling dice concievably forever. If you have enough Pyros and Pyros/Turn, you could concievably keep spending Pyros untill all your die has turned up a success.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T14:12:37-07:00","id":587413,"title":"","content":"And they're amongst the only splats able to <i>passively </i>regenerate their supernatural fuel. Got Hunters on your tail? Hide somewhere safe for a few days and you're back up and running","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T00:55:47-07:00","id":587916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/584478-a-bit-left-behind?p=587413#post587413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And they're amongst the only splats able to <i>passively </i>regenerate their supernatural fuel. Got Hunters on your tail? Hide somewhere safe for a few days and you're back up and running</div> </div> </div> </div>True dat.<br /> <br /> Prometheans have a high survivability rate with all their various benefits. The only real thing they got to watch out for is the centamani, angry mob/hunters, pandorans and their new antagonist...alchemists who want to harvest their parts and pyros.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6740-goblin-engineer","name":"Goblin Engineer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T15:53:23-07:00","id":588525,"title":"","content":"I still believe that alchemists can be more like fetches for the Lost. Not <i>entirely </i>antagonistic to the Created, certainly not helpful either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3857-kingme1","name":"Kingme1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T07:34:34-07:00","id":589176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kingme1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/584478-a-bit-left-behind?p=588525#post588525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still believe that alchemists can be more like fetches for the Lost. Not <i>entirely </i>antagonistic to the Created, certainly not helpful either.</div> </div> </div> </div>The setting and systems of the game dictate that any alliances/friendships will quickly dissolve, however. You've got orders of people who understand the physical aspects of what the Created are, and a mystical force that will inevitably force the alchemists to start hating the Prometheans that they hang out with.<br /> <br /> I mean, think about it: The alchemist knows that the Promethean is a corpse animated by the Divine Fire. The alchemist wants that Divine Fire. If they're a knowledgable, friendly alchemist, they might help a Promethean on their Pilgrimage, but how long until the alchemist sees the Created as nothing more than a walking bag of parts thanks to Disquiet? &quot;My need is greater than your right to exist/become human&quot;, &quot;They were never really alive to begin with&quot;, &quot;Your efforts to become human are selfish and cause more harm than good: I deserve what you have more than you do because I'll use it <i>right</i>&quot;, or &quot;You're wasting your gifts trying to become human: if you're just going to throw them away then I'll take them instead&quot;.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T09:58:22-07:00","id":589335,"title":"","content":"Here's for hoping that Disquiet is more maleable in 2nd edition - torches and pitchforks were somewhat bland in first. I always thought it would be nice for Disquieted people to rely solely on their Vice when interacting with Prometheans, and high-enough levels of disquiet spread that person's vice to others. So if you dealt with a Violent person for too long, you'll have a mob at your doorstep, but if you deal with Cowards, you'll have the police knocking at your door at every noise you make, since the neighbours are convinced that you're doing dangerous things. Dealing with Lusty people will get you an all other kind of violence, while dealing with Ambitious people would turn you into a slave like the Golem of myths.<br /> <br /> These are just examples, of course, but to get back to alchemists, it would allow for Prometheans to feel like their oppressor is right in some way. I'm not saying it's nice or that every Prometheans should, but if Disquiet does not equal angry mob of destruction, I think it opens up a lot of possibilities for stories. Is it really better alone than badly accompanied?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T07:34:05-07:00","id":590189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/584478-a-bit-left-behind?p=589335#post589335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's for hoping that Disquiet is more maleable in 2nd edition - torches and pitchforks were somewhat bland in first. I always thought it would be nice for Disquieted people to rely solely on their Vice when interacting with Prometheans, and high-enough levels of disquiet spread that person's vice to others. So if you dealt with a Violent person for too long, you'll have a mob at your doorstep, but if you deal with Cowards, you'll have the police knocking at your door at every noise you make, since the neighbours are convinced that you're doing dangerous things. Dealing with Lusty people will get you an all other kind of violence, while dealing with Ambitious people would turn you into a slave like the Golem of myths.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it'll be interesting to see how 2e's conditions cause Disquiet to be reworked. If there's one global change that I hope they make it's that other supernaturals are immune to Disquiet. Nothing made it harder to cross over Promethean than Disquiet. :/<br /> <br /> (Although the Wasteland effect also wasn't too helpful. It was easily enough nerfed by reducing its area of effects by an order of magnitude.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T08:10:39-07:00","id":590225,"title":"","content":"Significantly toning the ever present thorn at the side of the Created that is Disquiet would probably escape the themes of the line a bit. Removing it outright, even if only for crossover, would needless to say also remove a vital part of the Promethean condition that helps make them the tragic underdogs they are.<br /> <br /> I can understand the point of view, but personally I think it would miss something important. And I seem to recall Disquiet already had diminished or otherwise altered effects in most supernaturals in 1e?*<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">*Not super familiar with Promethean though, so I may have this wrong.</span><br /> <br /> Regardless, it's been explained that Disquiet and Wasteland are changing for Second Edition. It seems Disquiet will be more subtle and build up influenced by circumstances, and Wastelands won't ordinarily happen just by a Promethean staying in the same location for a moderate amount of time. The latter and the most severe consequences of the former can be triggered by great influxes of Pyros in the area, as well as specific conditions where a Promethean stretches or exceeds the allowances in interacting with people given by their progress in the Pilgrimage. The same events can also dramatically worsen both Disquiet and Wasteland.<br /> <br /> From what was said, the repercussions seem to have become more lenient at the most basic level, but at the same time also require conscious management and greater awareness of the part of the Prometheans to control and avoid the worst off. Which honestly was looking more interesting than how 1e did things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 07-14-2015, 11:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T08:31:44-07:00","id":590238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/584478-a-bit-left-behind?p=590225#post590225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can understand the point of view, but personally I think it would miss something important. And I seem to recall Disquiet already had diminished or otherwise altered effects in most supernaturals in 1e?*</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. Vampires and werewolves had penalties to resist their rage rather than a natural hate of the Promethean and Mages had an extra die of Paradox to all their spells if I remember correctly. I house-ruled a few tricks for the other Supers when I played a mixed-game.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T10:21:21-07:00","id":590285,"title":"","content":"Given that <i>Beast</i> explicitly calls out the Begotten as immune to the effects of Disquiet, I suspect that other supernaturals will get some sort of bonus or chance to resist rather than straight-up immunity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T11:22:04-07:00","id":590328,"title":"","content":"I certainly hope so. It was a little OtT for Prometheans to make Vamps and Werewolves perma-frenzy simply by existing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T19:48:39-07:00","id":590710,"title":"","content":"How was it out of theme? It meant that Prometheans were putting themselves even more in danger by standing near monsters than near mortals. It forsake them from <i>every kind </i>of society rather than only the mortal ones. Prometheans is not about cross-over, that's Beast's domain, so I don't mind supers naturally hating Prometheans (or frenzying, or spell-failing, or whatever). I actually think it fits the theme of Alienation a lot more than &quot;Humans hate them because they instinctively know they're not part of the natural order of this world, but Werewolves don't care.&quot;<br /> <br /> I won't get into why I still think Beasts should not like Prometheans, that's just a personal preference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T02:35:14-07:00","id":591028,"title":"","content":"Oh please don't make Promethean cross-over friendly. Not because I hate them, but because their whole disquiet effect made their plight unique. Why would a Promethean who can comfortably hang around a bunch of werewolves/beasts/changelings...ever go through with their pilgrimage to begin with? It would be like that one kid trying to fit in with the cool-kids (aka humans) when hes got a perfectly good group of friends (other supers) if that is what 2nd edition turns Promethean into.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6740-goblin-engineer","name":"Goblin Engineer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T12:01:15-07:00","id":591612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/584478-a-bit-left-behind?p=590710#post590710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How was it out of theme? It meant that Prometheans were putting themselves even more in danger by standing near monsters than near mortals. It forsake them from <i>every kind </i>of society rather than only the mortal ones. Prometheans is not about cross-over, that's Beast's domain, so I don't mind supers naturally hating Prometheans (or frenzying, or spell-failing, or whatever). I actually think it fits the theme of Alienation a lot more than &quot;Humans hate them because they instinctively know they're not part of the natural order of this world, but Werewolves don't care.&quot;<br /> <br /> I won't get into why I still think Beasts should not like Prometheans, that's just a personal preference.</div> </div> </div> </div>Over the Top not &quot;Out of Theme&quot;...<br /> <br /> I get that Promethean's central theme is alienation but alienation is a theme in all of the games. It doesn't really need to be taken to the nth degree just to make Promethean unique. IMO, a lot of mileage could be gotten out of a mechanic like -- innocents are immune to disquiet -- because it would act like the pinch of salt that brings out the alienation flavor to the fullest.<br /> <br /> Moreover it's a kludgey mechanic to deal with in cross-over settings. &quot;Because you exist&quot; is a deus ex machina raison d'\u00eatre for everyone hating on Prometheans. Most supernaturals have enough reason not to keep Prometheans around simply from their effect on mortals and the Wasteland effect. Having Disquiet also affect supernaturals detracts more from the game than it adds (takes the deck from being just stacked against the Promethean to being untenable). Recall that most supernaturals have shinsengumi levels of 'violence first, diplomacy later' for problem solving methods.<br /> <br /> As for Beasts, the way it's written now, there isn't any logical reason for any supernatural to like Beasts so their feelings of other supernaturals doesn't really seem that pertinent to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1630,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","user":"Jacob","date":". 07-15-2015, 03:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T12:11:37-07:00","id":591618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Goblin Engineer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/584478-a-bit-left-behind?p=591028#post591028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh please don't make Promethean cross-over friendly. Not because I hate them, but because their whole disquiet effect made their plight unique. Why would a Promethean who can comfortably hang around a bunch of werewolves/beasts/changelings...ever go through with their pilgrimage to begin with? It would be like that one kid trying to fit in with the cool-kids (aka humans) when hes got a perfectly good group of friends (other supers) if that is what 2nd edition turns Promethean into.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would they hang around one another? Recall that the alienation theme in Promethean is layered on so thickly that a game mechanic (i.e., a hack) had to be added to the rules to make group play even possible.<br /> <br /> More to your point though, like with my point about innocents above, if you want the sweetness of the cookies to come out to its fullest, don't be afraid to add a pinch of salt to the batch of cookie dough. The point of the pilgrimage is to become human, hanging out with other supernaturals (and being swept up in their drama) could be a distraction or it could be a necessity, it really depends on how the storyteller spins it. Cross-over should always be an option -- another tool in the tool box -- it shouldn't be something that is precluded by design. Some of us are going to do it anyway, shouldn't we have nice things too? I can be a fan of Promethean and be a fan of cross-over games both, can't I?<br /> <br /> This is an area were it's possible to eat the cake and still have it. Having options that are cross-over compatible doesn't detract from Promethean only games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T12:57:27-07:00","id":591646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/584478-a-bit-left-behind?p=591612#post591612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Beasts, the way it's written now, there isn't any logical reason for any supernatural to like Beasts so their feelings of other supernaturals doesn't really seem that pertinent to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Prometheans are probably the only group with a built in reason to like the Beasts. I was saying that the other way around should not be core.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Because you exist&quot; is a deus ex machina raison d'\u00eatre for everyone hating on Prometheans. Most supernaturals have enough reason not to keep Prometheans around simply from their effect on mortals and the Wasteland effect. </div> </div> </div>You realize you just said two completely opposite things right here? You stated that the Disquiet and the Wasteland are Deus Ex Machinas that should not exist, because the effects of such have repercusions which cause hate towards them from other supers. I understand that your point was to state that Prometheans can already be hated without having Disquiet affect supers, but then again what would such a thing tell Prometheans? &quot;Oh, sure, that bloodthirsty cadaver haunting the streets at night thinks you're a really nice guy. So does that shapeshifting beast of endless fury and that sorcerer mind-raping anyone in his vicinity. See? You're not hated at all!&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> hanging out with other supernaturals (and being swept up in their drama) could be a distraction or it could be a necessity, it really depends on how the storyteller spins it. Cross-over should always be an option -- another tool in the tool box -- it shouldn't be something that is precluded by design. Some of us are going to do it anyway, shouldn't we have nice things too? I can be a fan of Promethean and be a fan of cross-over games both, can't I? </div> </div> </div>You seem to misinterpret crossover games with cross-splat PCs. Disquiet and Wasteland and Flux is not a limit to crossover <i>elements,</i> it's a limit to crossover <i>play.</i> The big difference being that unless your players work out the details carefully, they can't simply start the game with &quot;A changeling, a Promethean and a Vamp get into a bar...&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I get that Promethean's central theme is alienation but alienation is a theme in all of the games. It doesn't really need to be taken to the nth degree just to make Promethean unique. </div> </div> </div>So by that logic, Beast &amp; Werewolves should not have to up the Family theme to 11 to be unique, nor should Mages be all about investigating and nor should Vamps be about the uncontrollable descent into inhumanity. All splats <i>can </i>use these themes, but honestly it's not their central theme. Mages do not suffer Alienation, they understand the world beyond what mortals can even pray to understand. Werewolves are not aliens, they are born in two worlds. Vamps are the ultimate predator but still understand what it means to be human (they simply dissociate from it).<br /> <br /> Prometheans woke up, fully adult, in a world they knew nothing about, a world that instinctively hates them for no reason they can understand, and yet a little voice in their head keeps telling them to keep going, that there is still hope, that if they take another step, it might work out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T13:08:14-07:00","id":591651,"title":"","content":"The best part about these games is don't use what you don't want. I have a wide diverse group that all have their one supernatural type they like and most of them would just rather not play then have to change to another type. So I always run mixed games or I run no games at all. <br /> That being said I like to use storytelling vs built in story hooks so I have removed a lot of the things that don't fit into my groups style of play. It takes next to no effort to do and as long as my players are fine with it so am I.<br /> So for the most part 80%+ of the negatives to supernatural a have been removed in our play style and the none human communities keep their own in check vs a built in system. I personally do not like the wasteland, disquiet and pilgrimage all together. So I have removed them. Prometheans are pretty much immortal creates as their creators created life but left out the death part and now they much search or a place to call their own in this world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6424-fuzzykuma","name":"Fuzzykuma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T13:18:21-07:00","id":591674,"title":"","content":"As long as you're all set up at the start and you all know what you're doing, it's fine. I played a mixed game where I (the only promethean player) was in <i>full control</i> of the disquiet and wasteland for the game and it was awesome because it was now a narrative device and I could choose how much of it I'd want to see used. Like you said &quot;Don't use what you don't like&quot;, but it's easier to remove than to add in these kinds of games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T13:48:03-07:00","id":591728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/584478-a-bit-left-behind?p=591646#post591646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prometheans are probably the only group with a built in reason to like the Beasts. I was saying that the other way around should not be core.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think we agree. IMO, Prometheans have no more reason to like any other supernatural than any other supernatural has to like any other supernatural but YMMV.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/584478-a-bit-left-behind?p=591646#post591646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You realize you just said two completely opposite things right here? You stated that the Disquiet and the Wasteland are Deus Ex Machinas that should not exist, because the effects of such have repercusions which cause hate towards them from other supers. I understand that your point was to state that Prometheans can already be hated without having Disquiet affect supers, but then again what would such a thing tell Prometheans? &quot;Oh, sure, that bloodthirsty cadaver haunting the streets at night thinks you're a really nice guy. So does that shapeshifting beast of endless fury and that sorcerer mind-raping anyone in his vicinity. See? You're not hated at all!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I must of missed that. ...could swear I only said it was &quot;the reason is 'because'&quot;. Not sure where you get me saying they shouldn't exist (at all). Deus ex machina is fine when used conservatively in very small doses. It's just another tool in the tool box. My point was that the existing 1st ed rules are over the top. I'm not the only person who finds the game's concepts to be phenomenal but the execution to be all but unplayable, take a look at the reviews out and about on the webs.<br /> <br /> I'm also not following your logic. Too much of something <i>is</i> a bad thing. If the game is totally hopeless then the Pilgrimage isn't going to be very interesting. It'll just be a one dimensional endurance fest. Having various exceptions to the Disquiet rule is the spice that adds dimensionality. What's more terrible, losing your sight or never having had vision in the first place? Right? Is it better to have loved and lost or to never have loved at all? &quot;Exceptions&quot; to the rules help bring these states of affairs about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/584478-a-bit-left-behind?p=591646#post591646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You seem to misinterpret crossover games with cross-splat PCs. Disquiet and Wasteland and Flux is not a limit to crossover <i>elements,</i> it's a limit to crossover <i>play.</i> The big difference being that unless your players work out the details carefully, they can't simply start the game with &quot;A changeling, a Promethean and a Vamp get into a bar...&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I simply don't understand what you're trying to say.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/584478-a-bit-left-behind?p=591646#post591646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So by that logic, Beast &amp; Werewolves should not have to up the Family theme to 11 to be unique, nor should Mages be all about investigating and nor should Vamps be about the uncontrollable descent into inhumanity. All splats <i>can </i>use these themes, but honestly it's not their central theme. Mages do not suffer Alienation, they understand the world beyond what mortals can even pray to understand. Werewolves are not aliens, they are born in two worlds. Vamps are the ultimate predator but still understand what it means to be human (they simply dissociate from it).</div> </div> </div> </div>And here you're simply willfully misinterpreting my words. I don't find Vampire, Werewolf, etc. rules to be OtT at all. That's not a position that I'd promulgate as none of their rules make their games all-but-unplayable. Promethean 1st ed on the other hand...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/584478-a-bit-left-behind?p=591646#post591646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prometheans woke up, fully adult, in a world they knew nothing about, a world that instinctively hates them for no reason they can understand, and yet a little voice in their head keeps telling them to keep going, that there is still hope, that if they take another step, it might work out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lol. This is not the sense of Promethean at all. They are rather compelled to just keep on trucking on even when all of the evidence points to inevitable failure. They're more like indestructible eeyores than anything resembling hopeful.<br /> <br /> When everything is stacked against you, when there is zero respite, well that's a bit of a problematic game and a problematic story. You need those intermittent breathing spaces to spice things up. That's just not the case with the current ruleset. You can't have a Lucy-football-Peanuts moment without the football.<br /> <br /> Now, it seems like many of these issues have been or are going to be addressed in second ed, so the meat of this conversation is quite likely moot and, I'm really looking forward to how 2nd ed shapes up.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T14:34:50-07:00","id":591790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/584478-a-bit-left-behind?p=591728#post591728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lol. This is not the sense of Promethean at all. They are rather compelled to just keep on trucking on even when all of the evidence points to inevitable failure. They're more like indestructible eeyores than anything resembling hopeful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, ok. If that's your view of Promethean: The Created we clearly won't be able to find common grounds to talk about. So on another note...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/584478-a-bit-left-behind?p=591728#post591728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, it seems like many of these issues have been or are going to be addressed in second ed, so the meat of this conversation is quite likely moot and, I'm really looking forward to how 2nd ed shapes up.</div> </div> </div> </div>YES. Let's pray it's completed as soon as possible so we can discuss the real meat of the game based on a new vision and writing!<br /> <br /> I drink to that!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T15:31:18-07:00","id":591942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/584478-a-bit-left-behind?p=591728#post591728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lol. This is not the sense of Promethean at all. They are rather compelled to just keep on trucking on even when all of the evidence points to inevitable failure. They're more like indestructible eeyores than anything resembling hopeful.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, I mean, Prometheans are one of the few supernaturals with a clear, theoretically achievable &quot;happy ending&quot; possible for them. I mean, yeah, Changelings escaped their captors...to a life of fear and paranoia; Demons can achieve Hell. Maybe. And it won't necessarily be what they intended. Prometheans are about the only splat where they can truly hang up their sad hats and say &quot;I did it. Time to retire.&quot;<br /> <br /> Nobody else gets to do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T16:04:24-07:00","id":591972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/584478-a-bit-left-behind?p=591942#post591942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dunno, I mean, Prometheans are one of the few supernaturals with a clear, theoretically achievable &quot;happy ending&quot; possible for them. I mean, yeah, Changelings escaped their captors...to a life of fear and paranoia; Demons can achieve Hell. Maybe. And it won't necessarily be what they intended. Prometheans are about the only splat where they can truly hang up their sad hats and say &quot;I did it. Time to retire.&quot;<br /> <br /> Nobody else gets to do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mummies?<br /> <br /> Interesting that it's a thing in common between the game lines closest to the &quot;childhood&quot; and &quot;old age&quot; ends of the scale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T16:44:36-07:00","id":592038,"title":"","content":"Hunters, by definition, can retire. So can Heroes, if they manage to hold onto their Integrity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T20:42:40-07:00","id":592266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/584478-a-bit-left-behind?p=591972#post591972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mummies?<br /> <br /> Interesting that it's a thing in common between the game lines closest to the &quot;childhood&quot; and &quot;old age&quot; ends of the scale.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/584478-a-bit-left-behind?p=592038#post592038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunters, by definition, can retire. So can Heroes, if they manage to hold onto their Integrity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Touche, but still, the splats that can hang up their splat hat are in the minority.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T07:04:21-07:00","id":592588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/584478-a-bit-left-behind?p=591942#post591942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dunno, I mean, Prometheans are one of the few supernaturals with a clear, theoretically achievable &quot;happy ending&quot; possible for them. I mean, yeah, Changelings escaped their captors...to a life of fear and paranoia; Demons can achieve Hell. Maybe. And it won't necessarily be what they intended. Prometheans are about the only splat where they can truly hang up their sad hats and say &quot;I did it. Time to retire.&quot;<br /> <br /> Nobody else gets to do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's all very good in theory but the realities of gameplay work out differently. It's a soulcrushing slog to actually achieve the so-called &quot;happy ending&quot;.<br /> <br /> The problem that the left and right hooks of Disquiet and Wasteland lead to very rinse and repeat type of storytelling where the character(s) is(are) safe in one place for a little while before inevitably having to move again. Hypothetically this is fine if one wants a BSG-like game; however, even a show like BSG is essentially about the connections that the characters make to one another and the people they're traveling with. Promethean 1st ed does(did) not have this kind of added dimensionality. There's no pressure release valve.<br /> <br /> Very few players want to play a game that in essence is an analogy for what it's like to suffer from depression, except of course the game has zero up moments so it's even worse than actual depression. Even when you have such a rarefied troupe (and more likely it's just one player in your troupe) that is willing to take on the challenge the game has zero upbeats where the end goal actually seems achievable. It's basically a race to see if you character(s) can get off of the merry-go-round of doom before they face-plant into the bottom of the abyss like a lawn dart (F-16) with engine failure.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I'm looking forward to a system that makes the end the goal more achievable but also throws in more distractors that can lure / divert characters off of their pilgrimages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T08:08:26-07:00","id":592633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/584478-a-bit-left-behind?p=592588#post592588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So yeah, I'm looking forward to a system that makes the end the goal more achievable but also throws in more distractors that can lure / divert characters off of their pilgrimages.</div> </div> </div> </div>I rather like the Disquiet and Wasteland dynamic as it is now. If I really want to do a big crossover game with Prometheans, I'll make the relevant other splats immune to Disquiet and add some ways to remove Wasteland that don't include leaving the area for a while. Much like I removed Compromise checks when dealing with Vampires or Ghouls in a Vampire/Demon crossover game.<br /> <br /> But for a pure Promethean game, the core of &quot;You need to learn about humanity, and that means interacting with them, but interacting with them is dangerous and you'll probably get yourself and others hurt, possibly even killed.&quot;<br /> <br /> In other words, what you think made the game unplayable I thought was a feature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T11:11:23-07:00","id":592935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/584478-a-bit-left-behind?p=592588#post592588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's all very good in theory but the realities of gameplay work out differently. It's a soulcrushing slog to actually achieve the so-called &quot;happy ending&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>YMMV, because in my 3 chronicles my players found many ways to let go of the pressure and even existed in the same city for a long time by each having a same place at different spots in town and shifting between those. Promethean is the kind of game that turns abandoned places from depressing to welcoming. Internet helps prometheans keep contact with mortals as do phones or even small interactions. A Ferrum climbing a mountain and seeing the sun rise once he's on top can take it as a pause. An Aurum that scores a short contract job is doing fine. A Cuprum who takes care of a rare plant in the forest, making sure to stay as little as possible and one day finds it bloomed. A Vulcanus who discovers a written Ramble. Disquiet and Wasteland are narrative effects created to force the players to think differently about the little things.<br /> <br /> You can't play Prometheans as you would Vampire or Mage, but that's a feature as BigHero said.<br /> <br /> Disquiet is slow and insidious. It's made this way specifically to allow &quot;good&quot; moments of pressure-dropping before going back to the core of the game. It's not (as too many think) an instant punch in the face from every mortal you encounter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T13:47:09-07:00","id":593110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/584478-a-bit-left-behind?p=592935#post592935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Internet helps prometheans keep contact with mortals as do phones or even small interactions.</div> </div> </div> </div>No jokes, I once had a Nepri who was a world-class Starcraft player. He even got a few milestones out of tournament play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T14:07:25-07:00","id":593129,"title":"","content":"A player of mine decided to play a wandering musician with a dot of fame. Since the only interaction he had with people was a one-night-long show once in a while, people loved him.<br /> I played a Frankenstein gardener who worked on contracts. Dealt with people for a single week and then was off, his business done.<br /> Another player went for a private-investigator Tammuz, no one likes the PI investigating their life anyway <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Prometheans are awesome - if you accept the episodic nature of their existence","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T11:15:59-07:00","id":594870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/584478-a-bit-left-behind?p=592935#post592935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't play Prometheans as you would Vampire or Mage...</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of the charm\u2014or the sense of dread, as some may think\u2014of <b>Promethean</b> is the lack of clear narrative archetype. I mean, sure you can point at <i>Frankenstein</i>, but that book doesn't have any kind of proper ending for the Creature; he just wanders off into the ice to dispose of the carcass of his creator. At least with your Dracula or Edward Cullen, there's some kind of 'he did something that led to something' sort of narrative. I don't want it to sound like I think this isn't a problem with other World of Darkness games (pardon the double-negative), but when coupled with the fact that the Pilgrimage DOES have a possible ending point, <b>Promethean</b> looks like an odd duck, indeed.<br /> <br /> I so want Second Edition to come out, as the hints so far have been kind of wonderful, and I'm pleased that others feel the same way. My words above notwithstanding, this thread has quite raised my hopes for the future of <b>Promethean: the Created</b>, so thank you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}